simulated column: 12 of 15 exact matches; all deltas within the noise of a 2e6-round simulation at a 5e-6 tail (see the monotonicity note)

### Hill's own table is non-monotonic, which bounds its simulation noise
A lower min entropy means a larger p and therefore a cutoff that cannot be smaller.
- H_I 1.9908 -> 317 and H_I 2 -> 318 (simulated): non-monotonic by 1
- H_I 3.97586 -> 105 and H_I 4 -> 104 (simulated): monotonic
- H_I 14.3163 -> 5 and H_I 16 -> 4 (simulated): monotonic

